-- Export the three functions with CommonJS while keeping browser use possible.
+## 1. Experience (What the user lives)
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+**When** a reviewer is looking at pending items, the reviewer wants to select exactly the items they intend to approve, **so that** approval is deliberate and no unselected item changes status.
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As a reviewer, I want to select pending items and approve only that selection so that I can make a confident, reversible choice before confirmation.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality (How the user feels)
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Review list | Cautious | In control of exactly what will be approved | Surprise, ambiguity, accidental confirmation |
+
+### 1d. Magic Moments Tied to This Story
+
+No project-level magic moments are defined in this workspace; `serves` therefore remains empty.
+
+## 2. Acceptance LARP (How we prove the experience works)
+
+### 2a. Required Personas to LARP
+
+| Persona | Flow | Build artifact | Evidence required |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| reviewer | Select and approve review items | Local browser page | DOM inspection and automated state-transition tests |
+
+### 2b. Acceptance Scenarios
+
+#### AC-1 — Initialize a safe pending review state
+- **GIVEN** a list of uniquely identified input items
+- **WHEN** `initialState(items)` is called
+- **THEN** it returns a new state whose items are pending and unselected, without changing the input items
+- **EVIDENCE** `test/review-state.test.js` initialization and immutability assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-2 — Select and unselect only the requested item
+- **GIVEN** an initialized review state
+- **WHEN** `toggleSelection(state, id)` is called with a known id
+- **THEN** only that item’s selection flips and all other item values remain intact
+- **AND** an unknown id returns the original state unchanged
+- **EVIDENCE** `test/review-state.test.js` selection assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-3 — Approve exactly the selected items
+- **GIVEN** a review state with selected and unselected pending items
+- **WHEN** `approveSelected(state)` is called
+- **THEN** selected items become confirmed, unselected statuses remain unchanged, and every item is unselected afterward
+- **AND** when nothing is selected it returns the original state unchanged
+- **EVIDENCE** `test/review-state.test.js` approval assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-4 — Make the selection state accessible in the browser
+- **GIVEN** the browser review controls are rendered
+- **WHEN** a reviewer examines the controls
+- **THEN** each item button reflects its exact selection with `aria-pressed` and Approve is disabled with no selection
+- **EVIDENCE** `test/review-state.test.js` source-level browser-control contract assertion
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
