+# UI Specification: Review selection state
+
+**Story**: S007-review-state  
+**Epic**: E001-capture-review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-11  
+**Version**: 1.0
+
+## Design Context Sources
+
+No design system, UX strategy, wireframes, recipe, or declared PROFILE surface exists in this workspace. The implementation uses the existing static page and semantic browser controls; a project design system should be added before a broader visual surface is built.
+
+## PROFILE surface impact
+
+- [x] No
+
+## Visual Assets Requirements
+
+- [x] No
+
+## Component Overview
+
+**Component Name**: Review selection controls  
+**Type**: Modified static-page control set  
+**Affects**: `web/index.html` review list and Approve action
+
+## Visual Specifications
+
+### Component Anatomy
+
+```
+Review list
+├── Item button (one per item, aria-pressed reflects selection)
+└── Approve button (disabled until one or more items are selected)
+```
+
+### Visual Properties
+
+- Use native buttons with a 2px high-contrast focus outline.
+- Selected items use a dark background and light foreground; unselected items use a light surface and dark foreground.
+- Buttons use 10px vertical / 14px horizontal padding, 8px radius, and a 120ms background/transform transition.
+- On hover, lift 1px; on active, return to baseline. Respect reduced motion.
+
+## States & Behavior
+
+| State | Item button | Approve button |
+|---|---|---|
+| No selection | `aria-pressed="false"` | disabled |
+| Selected | `aria-pressed="true"` | enabled |
+| After approval | all `aria-pressed="false"`; selected statuses confirmed | disabled unless a new item is selected |
+
+There are no forms or text inputs, so a field-validation matrix is not applicable.
+
+## Interactions
+
+- Click / Enter / Space: native button activation toggles an item or approves the current selection.
+- Tab: follows DOM order through item controls and then Approve.
+- Touch: tap has the same behavior as click.
+- No loading or error state is needed because transitions are synchronous and local; duplicate ids are rejected before rendering.
+
+## Density Budget & Responsive Behavior
+
+- One screen, one job: select review items and approve the selected set.
+- Mobile, tablet, and desktop: items wrap naturally; touch targets remain at least 44px high.
+
+## Accessibility Requirements
+
+- Native `<button>` elements provide keyboard activation.
+- Each item has its visible item label and a truthful `aria-pressed` state.
+- The native disabled attribute prevents premature approval.
+- Focus uses a visible 2px outline with at least 3:1 contrast.
+
+## Testing Checklist
+
+- [x] Selected and unselected control state maps to `aria-pressed`.
+- [x] Approve is disabled until selection exists.
+- [x] Keyboard activation is supported by native buttons.
+- [x] Focus and selected visual states are present in the static-page stylesheet.
